    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d837">

                <pb facs="0915" n="1749" xml:id="pg1749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/380</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >DeBillier</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-11T22:00:00-04:42">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1918, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 12, 6.37 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s April 10, 5 p.m. Foreign Office very appreciative of generous
                    attitude of United States towards lease of German vessels and says boats would
                    be officered and manned as are the Chilean transports. Likewise unreservedly
                    consents as to enemy passengers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">DeBillier</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
